lity":true,"_score_rev_volatility":100.0,"_gate_margin_vs_hist":0.0530788097728673,"_gp_margin_vs_hist":false,"_score_margin_vs_hist":33.7,"_gate_piotroski":6,"_gp_piotroski":false,"_score_piotroski":66.7,"_gate_spread":null,"_gp_spread":null,"_score_spread":null,"_gate_roic_consistency":null,"_gp_roic_consistency":null,"_score_roic_consistency":null,"_gate_incr_roic":null,"_gp_incr_roic":null,"_score_incr_roic":null,"_gate_margin_advantage":null,"_gp_margin_advantage":null,"_score_margin_advantage":null,"_gate_pool_share":-0.0006230384202499106,"_gp_pool_share":false,"_score_pool_share":39.8,"_gate_rev_durability":0.04757517157165281,"_gp_rev_durability":true,"_score_rev_durability":48.8,"_gate_fcf_durability":null,"_gp_fcf_durability":null,"_score_fcf_durability":null,"_gate_margins":null,"_gp_margins":null,"_score_margins":null,"_gate_fund_growth":null,"_gp_fund_growth":null,"_score_fund_growth":null,"_gate_shrhldr_yield":0.06768661924562147,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":true,"_score_shrhldr_yield":86.3,"_gate_share_shrink":-0.03327194386702814,"_gp_share_shrink":true,"_score_share_shrink":91.6,"_gate_sbc_dilution":0.008900929179933396,"_gp_sbc_dilution":true,"_score_sbc_dilution":85.2,"_gate_insider_own":0.0069700005,"_gp_insider_own":false,"_score_insider_own":4.6,"_gate_insider_buying":0.0,"_gp_insider_buying":false,"_score_insider_buying":0.0,"pf":[],"description_full":"Globe Life Inc., through its subsidiaries, provides various life and supplemental health insurance products to lower middle- and middle-income families in the United States. It operates in three segments: Life Insurance, Supplemental Health Insurance, and Investments. The company offers whole, term, and other life insurance products, as well as life insurance for children; Medicare supplement and limited-benefit supplemental health insurance products, such as accident, cancer, critical illness, heart, intensive care, and other health products; and final expense, accidental death, mortgage protection, and hospital insurance products. It sells its products through direct-to-consumer channels, exclusive independent agents, general agency independent agents, and brokers. The company was formerly known as Torchmark Corporation and changed its name to Globe Life Inc. in August 2019. Globe Life Inc. was founded in 1900 and is headquartered in McKinney, Texas.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Frank Martin Svoboda | Co-Chairman & Co-CEO | Age 63 | Compensation: $2.7M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 3K people. Revenue per employee of $1.6M ranks in the top quartile among Financial Services peers. Each employee generates $339K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $14K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 2\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags elevated compensation governance risk (9/10).","financial_summary":["Globe Life Inc. is a large-cap financial services business with a $11.9B market cap on $6.0B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +5% over the past three years and +5% annually across the full decade, which puts it in mature, slow-growth territory.","Returns on capital run at 15% against a 7% cost of capital, a 8-point spread that creates value, though narrow enough that competitive pressure could close it, and 20% gross margins are typical of commodity economics where competitors can replicate the product cheaply.","The business throws off $1.3B in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 21 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 1.20\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, leverage is comfortably conservative at 1.6\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and interest coverage runs at 11.2\u00d7.","Management returns a meaningful 6.8% of market cap to owners through dividends and buybacks, a strong signal of disciplined capital allocation, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (1.0) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Insiders are net sellers (100% sell ratio, net $39.7M) \u2014 the people closest to the business are reducing their personal stake","sev":"amber","cat":"insider"},{"text":"Above-average market volatility (VIX 26)","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Late-cycle dynamics increase the probability of a slowdown","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Credit cycles and regulatory capital \u2014 losses accumulate invisibly in good years and appear all at once, and the time to worry is when underwriting standards are loosest.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Fintech disintermediation \u2014 neobanks, embedded finance, and blockchain rails are unbundling the fee streams that traditional banks took for granted.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Interest rate regime shifts \u2014 a rapid move in rates can invert the yield curve, crush bond portfolios, and trigger deposit flight simultaneously.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Trading at a 44% margin of safety to estimated fair value \u2014 a real cushion against errors in the estimate","Market is pricing in lower growth than the company has historically delivered","39 consecutive years of dividend payments \u2014 an operating record that makes the dividend claim credible","Healthy payout ratio leaves room for both dividend growth and reinvestment","Minimal goodwill on the balance sheet \u2014 low impairment risk"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Zylox-Tonbridge and GL Capital Announce Strategic Investment in LifeTech Scientific to Build a Leading Vascular and Structural Heart Intervention Platform","source